Job Requisition ID: 181887 

 About Al-Futtaim 

 Established in the 1930s, Al-Futtaim is one of the most diversified and progressive privately held regional businesses, headquartered in Dubai. Operating across more than 20 countries, the Group spans automotive, financial services, real estate, retail and health. With more than 40,000 employees, Al-Futtaim represents over 200 of the world’s most recognised brands, including Toyota, Lexus, IKEA, ACE and Marks & Spencer. Driven by its purpose to enrich lives and elevate communities, Al-Futtaim focuses on digital innovation, AI, sustainable growth and strategic partnerships, creating long-term value for customers, communities and partners while building a responsible legacy for future generations. 

 Job Purpose 

 To support the placement of Property facultative reinsurance by preparing accurate reinsurance submissions, approaching approved reinsurance markets, obtaining competitive capacity and terms, and completing placement documentation within required timelines. 

 The role will coordinate closely with property underwriters, brokers, reinsurers, risk engineers, finance, claims, and policy administration teams to ensure that facultative placements comply with the company’s underwriting appetite, treaty requirements, delegated authority limits, regulatory obligations, and internal procedures. 

 Key Responsibilities 

 Facultative Reinsurance Placement 

 Review underwriting referrals requiring facultative reinsurance support. 

 Understand the required facultative structure, including: 

 Sum insured and probable maximum loss; 

 Company retention; 

 Treaty capacity; 

 Facultative capacity required; 

 Quota share or excess-of-loss structure; 

 Layers, deductibles and limits; 

 Brokerage, commission and applicable taxes; 

 Placement currency and premium allocation. 

 Prepare clear and complete facultative reinsurance submissions for Property and related risks. 

 Approach approved local, regional and international reinsurance markets. 

 Follow up with reinsurers and brokers to obtain quotations and capacity within agreed timelines. 

 Negotiate reinsurance rates, commissions, coverage, exclusions, warranties and other placement conditions under the supervision of senior underwriters. 

 Prepare quotation comparisons and recommend commercially and technically suitable placement options. 

 Maintain accurate records of all market approaches, quotations, declinatures and placement status. 

 Secure written reinsurance confirmation before the company commits to facultative-dependent risks. 

 Ensure that the final placement provides the required capacity and follows the approved underwriting structure. 

 Technical 

 Review available underwriting information, including: 

 COPE information; 

 Risk survey reports; 

 Claims experience; 

 Fire protection systems; 

 Natural catastrophe exposure; 

 Valuation reports; 

 Policy wording and requested extensions. 

 Identify missing, inconsistent or inadequate underwriting information before approaching the reinsurance market. 

 Highlight material exposures, including fire, explosion, machinery breakdown, natural catastrophe, contingent business interruption and accumulation risks. 

 Review reinsurers’ quotations to identify differences in coverage, pricing, deductibles, exclusions, warranties and subjectivities. 

 Escalate technical issues, capacity shortages, restrictive terms or material coverage gaps to the relevant senior underwriter. 

 Placement 

 Prepare and maintain: 

 Facultative slips; 

 Reinsurance submissions; 

 Comparison sheets where required; 

 Signing and placement schedules; 

 Reinsurance confirmations; 

 Cover notes; 

 Closing instructions; 

 Premium calculation sheets; 

 Endorsement requests; 

 Renewal and expiry records. 

 Ensure that all reinsurer subjectivities are recorded, communicated and completed within the required timeframe. 

 Maintain a complete audit trail of correspondence, approvals and placement evidence. 

 Renewals 

 Maintain an updated diary of facultative renewals and initiate the placement process sufficiently in advance. 

 Coordinate with underwriting teams to obtain updated risk information and renewal instructions. 

 Monitor changes in exposures, claims experience, sums insured, business interruption values and risk improvements. 

 Track outstanding confirmations, subjectivities, premium closings and documentation. 

 Identify renewals that may face capacity, pricing or timing challenges and escalate them promptly. 

 Support periodic analysis of facultative premium, capacity utilization, reinsurer participation and placement performance. 

 Coordination 

 Coordinate with property underwriters to understand the risk, proposed terms and required reinsurance structure. 

 Liaise professionally with reinsurers, reinsurance brokers and internal stakeholders. 

 Provide regular updates on placement progress, outstanding requirements and market feedback. 

 Assist underwriting teams in responding to technical queries raised by reinsurers. 

 Maintain effective working relationships with approved reinsurance markets. 

 Coordinate with finance and reinsurance accounting teams regarding premium closings, settlements and outstanding balances. 

 Support claims teams in obtaining reinsurer notifications, confirmations or documentation when required. 

 Compliance and Governance 

 Follow the company’s underwriting guidelines, reinsurance security requirements, authority limits and referral procedures. 

 Place business only with approved reinsurers and brokers, unless otherwise authorized. 

 Ensure compliance with applicable sanctions, KYC, AML and regulatory requirements. 

 Maintain confidentiality of client, underwriting and reinsurance information. 

 Ensure that no facultative-dependent risk is bound without documented reinsurance support and the required internal approval. 

 Support internal, external and regulatory audits by providing accurate placement records and supporting documentation. 

 Report any conflict of interest, compliance concern or documentation discrepancy through the appropriate internal channel. 

 Work Experience – 5 years and regional experience will be an advantage 

 Qualification: Bachelor’s degree in insurance, Risk Management, Business Administration, Finance, Economics, Engineering, or a related discipline. 

 Professional Qualifications: Diploma or Advances Diploma form III or CII shall be considered as added qualification 

 About Orient Insurance PJSC 

 Orient Insurance Company commenced operations in 1982 as a part of the reputed Al-Futtaim Group and has since recorded a progressively steady growth. The Company is counted among the leaders in the UAE insurance market. Orient Insurance Company has a paid-up capital of AED 500 Million which is the highest in the insurance industry in UAE. With head office in Dubai, the company serves its clientele through an extensive branch network in Jebel Ali, Abu Dhabi, Al Ain, Sharjah and Ras Al Khaimah in UAE, Muscat in Sultanate of Oman, Riyadh in Kingdom of Saudi Arabia and Bahrain. 

